{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:15:20Z","thinking":"**Initiating Walkthrough Documentation**\n\nDetermining the appropriate content and format for the `walkthrough.md` artifact. The document will summarize completed work, focusing on changes made, testing conducted, and validation results. This approach helps in documenting the work done, as well as enabling easier follow-ups and further work.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Walkthrough document detailing the completed implementation of the offline password manager web app, cryptographic design, IndexedDB storage, and usage options.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Offline Password Manager - Walkthrough\n\nA 100% offline, zero-backend, zero-network password manager web application built with React, the browser's native **Web Crypto API** (PBKDF2 + AES-GCM 256-bit), and **IndexedDB**.\n\n## Summary of Accomplishments\n\n1. **Security & Cryptography Architecture (`src/services/crypto.js`)**:\n   - **Key Derivation**: Uses PBKDF2 with SHA-256 and 100,000 iterations seeded with a cryptographically secure 16-byte random salt (`crypto.getRandomValues`).\n   - **Data Encryption**: Authenticated AES-GCM 256-bit encryption with a unique 12-byte initialization vector (IV) generated for each entry.\n   - **Zero-Knowledge Auth**: Master password correctness is validated by attempting to decrypt a canary token (`__OFFLINE_VAULT_CANARY_OK__`). No password hash is ever saved.\n   - **Memory Hygiene**: Master keys exist strictly in volatile RAM and are destroyed immediately when the vault is locked or upon inactivity timeout.\n\n2. **Local Persistence Layer (`src/services/db.js`)**:\n   - Built a native IndexedDB database (`OfflinePasswordManagerDB`) with two object stores:\n     - `meta`: Holds vault salt, verification canary, and auto-lock preferences.\n     - `items`: Holds encrypted records (`ciphertext`, `iv`, `category`, `favorite`, `updatedAt`).\n   - Zero external storage or ORM dependencies.\n\n3. **User Interface & State Management**:\n   - **`src/context/VaultContext.jsx`**: Global vault state management, auto-lock timeout detector, CRUD operations, re-encryption on master password change, and encrypted backup export/import.\n   - **`src/components/UnlockScreen.jsx`**: Initial master password configuration with password entropy meter and lock screen with error animations.\n   - **`src/components/Navbar.jsx`**: Top navigation with instant search, lock button, generator trigger, and security health indicator.\n   - **`src/components/Sidebar.jsx`**: Category filtering (All, Logins, Cards, Notes, Favorites) with live item counters and offline status indicator.\n   - **`src/components/ItemList.jsx` & `ItemCard.jsx`**: Responsive grid of credentials with one-click copy, password mask/reveal toggles, and category icons.\n   - **`src/components/ItemModal.jsx`**: Modal for creating and editing credentials with an inline password generator and strength evaluator.\n   - **`src/components/PasswordGeneratorModal.jsx`**: Standalone cryptographically secure generator with customizable length (8-64) and character set toggles.\n   - **`src/components/SecurityAuditModal.jsx`**: Proactive audit tool identifying weak passwords (< 12 characters) and duplicate/reused passwords across different services.\n   - **`src/components/SettingsModal.jsx`**: Configurable auto-lock timer, master password change (with full vault re-encryption), encrypted backup download/import, and factory reset.\n\n4. **Zero-Network Content Security Policy**:\n   - Configured CSP: `default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data:; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';`\n   - With `connect-src 'none'`, the browser enforces that no fetch, XHR, WebSocket, or remote calls can ever be made.\n\n5. **Dual Delivery Modes**:\n   - **Modular React + Vite Codebase** in `src/` for standard development and building (`npm run dev`).\n   - **Self-Contained Standalone Edition** in `offline-vault.html` that can be directly opened in any browser (Edge, Chrome, Firefox) without running terminal commands or installing dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## File Overview\n\n| File | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| [offline-vault.html](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/offline-vault.html) | Standalone single-file edition ready to run immediately in any browser |\n| [README.md](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/README.md) | Full project documentation and security architecture |\n| [index.html](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/index.html) | Vite entry HTML with strict zero-network CSP |\n| [package.json](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/package.json) | React 18 and Vite configuration |\n| [vite.config.js](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/vite.config.js) | Vite dev server and build configuration |\n| [src/services/crypto.js](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/services/crypto.js) | Native Web Crypto API (PBKDF2 + AES-GCM) implementation |\n| [src/services/db.js](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/services/db.js) | Native IndexedDB storage wrapper |\n| [src/services/generator.js](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/services/generator.js) | Cryptographically secure random password generator |\n| [src/context/VaultContext.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/context/VaultContext.jsx) | Global vault state, encryption, auto-lock & sync |\n| [src/components/Icons.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/Icons.jsx) | Local SVG icons with zero network requests |\n| [src/components/UnlockScreen.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/UnlockScreen.jsx) | Setup & Unlock screen with entropy meter |\n| [src/components/Navbar.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/Navbar.jsx) | Header bar with search and quick actions |\n| [src/components/Sidebar.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/Sidebar.jsx) | Category navigation and offline indicator |\n| [src/components/ItemList.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/ItemList.jsx) | Credential grid and category filter list |\n| [src/components/ItemCard.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/ItemCard.jsx) | Credential display with one-click copy |\n| [src/components/ItemModal.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/ItemModal.jsx) | Add/Edit modal with inline generator |\n| [src/components/PasswordGeneratorModal.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/PasswordGeneratorModal.jsx) | Standalone password generator |\n| [src/components/SecurityAuditModal.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/SecurityAuditModal.jsx) | Weak and reused password detector |\n| [src/components/SettingsModal.jsx](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/src/components/SettingsModal.jsx) | Auto-lock, password change, backup/restore |\n\n---\n\n## How to Access & Verify\n\n### Quickest Way: Run `offline-vault.html`\n1. Navigate to: `C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager`\n2. Double-click [`offline-vault.html`](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/offline-vault.html) to open it in Microsoft Edge, Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Brave.\n3. Set your Master Password on first launch.\n4. Add credentials, generate strong passwords, test one-click copy, and check the Health Audit tab.\n5. Open browser Developer Tools (F12) -> **Network tab**: Observe **0 HTTP/HTTPS requests** being made.\n\n### Running with Vite\nIf you prefer running via the Vite dev server:\n```bash\ncd C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\nNavigate to `http://localhost:3000`.\n","Description":"Create walkthrough artifact for the completed offline password manager","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\0fddf4ef-d93f-406e-8ec9-d51e8406f759\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Creating walkthrough.md","toolSummary":"Create walkthrough.md"}}]}
