{"step_index":75,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:16:45Z","content":"**Yes, you can easily run it in VS Code!** \n\nPre-configured VS Code settings ([`launch.json`](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/.vscode/launch.json) and [`tasks.json`](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/.vscode/tasks.json)) have been added to the project directory.\n\nHere is how to run it:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Open the Project Folder in VS Code\n1. Launch **Visual Studio Code**.\n2. Go to **File** > **Open Folder...** (or press `Ctrl + K, Ctrl + O`).\n3. Select this folder:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Choose How You Want to Run\n\n#### Method A: Using VS Code Integrated Terminal (Recommended)\n1. Open the terminal in VS Code: press **`Ctrl + \\``** (or go to **Terminal** > **New Terminal**).\n2. Run:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n3. `Ctrl + Click` the local link shown in the terminal (e.g., `http://localhost:3000`).\n\n---\n\n#### Method B: One-Click Task (Built into VS Code)\n1. In VS Code, press **`Ctrl + Shift + B`** (Run Build Task).\n2. It will automatically start `npm: dev`.\n\n---\n\n#### Method C: Without Node.js (Using the VS Code \"Live Server\" Extension)\nIf you have the **Live Server** extension in VS Code:\n1. In the file explorer sidebar on the left, right-click [`offline-vault.html`](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/offline-vault.html).\n2. Select **\"Open with Live Server\"**.\n\n---\n\n### View Directly Inside VS Code (Optional)\nTo preview the app without switching to an external browser:\n1. Press `Ctrl + Shift + P`.\n2. Type and select **`Simple Browser: Show`**.\n3. Enter `http://localhost:3000`.","thinking":"**Outlining VS Code Execution Steps**\n\nThe user needs specific steps to launch the application within the VS Code environment.  First, the correct folder must be opened using the \"Open Folder\" command. Next, the user can start the development server using the VS Code terminal. Ensure that the dependencies are installed via a command prior to running the server command.\n\n\n"}
