{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:21:14Z","content":"Here is the exact step-by-step guide to run and use your password manager right now:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Open the App\n\nPick whichever method is easier for you:\n\n#### Option A: Immediate (No commands or setup needed)\n1. Press `Win + E` to open Windows File Explorer.\n2. Paste this into the address bar and press **Enter**:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager\n   ```\n3. Double-click [`offline-vault.html`](file:///C:/Users/vijay/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/offline-password-manager/offline-vault.html).\n4. It will open immediately in your default browser (Chrome, Edge, or Firefox).\n\n---\n\n#### Option B: In VS Code (Vite Dev Server)\n1. Open **VS Code**.\n2. Click **File** > **Open Folder...** and select:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager\n   ```\n3. Open the VS Code terminal by pressing **`Ctrl + \\``** (or click **Terminal** > **New Terminal**).\n4. Type this command and press Enter (first time only):\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n5. Once that finishes, start the app:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n6. Click the link that appears in the terminal (usually `http://localhost:3000`).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: First-Time Setup (In the Browser)\n\nWhen the app opens:\n\n1. **Set your Master Password**:\n   - Type a strong master password (at least 8 characters).\n   - Retype it in the confirm field.\n   > [!IMPORTANT]\n   > Remember this password. Because the app is 100% offline and zero-knowledge, there are no cloud servers to reset a lost password.\n2. Click **\"Create Secure Vault\"**.\n   - The browser uses the native Web Crypto API to derive an AES-256-GCM encryption key and stores your vault locally in IndexedDB.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add and Test Your Credentials\n\n1. **Add an entry**:\n   - Click the blue **\"+ New Item\"** button in the top right.\n   - Select category (**Login**, **Card**, or **Note**).\n   - Enter a Title (e.g., `GitHub` or `Gmail`).\n   - Fill in your username and password, or click **\"✨ Generate Strong\"** to create a cryptographically secure random password automatically.\n   - Click **\"Encrypt & Save\"**.\n2. **Copy Credentials**:\n   - On the item card, click the **Clipboard icon (📋)** next to username or password to copy it with one click.\n   - Click the **Eye icon (👁️)** to reveal or hide the password.\n3. **Verify Security & Offline Nature**:\n   - Click **\"Health\"** in the top bar to run a security audit (scans for weak or duplicate passwords).\n   - Click **\"Lock\"** in the top bar: the master key is immediately erased from memory.\n   - Press **F12** to open browser Developer Tools -> click the **Network tab** -> observe that **0 network requests** are sent. Everything stays strictly inside your device.","thinking":"**Defining Project Initialization Steps**\n\nThe user needs a clear project startup guide after creation. This calls for breaking down the process into actionable steps on a Windows OS, given the provided project path. The primary goal is to get the project operational.\n\n\n"}
